mental feelings that  they have on a number of different  issues and you're not going to be able  to sort of talk out a compromise with a  lot of people on a lot of these  important  issues so what exactly does being a  centrist get you in that context I don't  think very much there are issues where  centrism and compromise is possible  immigration would be an idea on  immigration you actually might be able  to get some kind of centrist compromise  and maybe it would be reasonable to do  that  overall I see it as an unpretentious and  objective breaking news just being in  the middle on an issue doesn't make you  any less biased or more objective than  having a more politically polarized  position it could be the right position  it could be the wrong position you could  have it for genuine reasons or  disingenuous reasons but there's nothing  uniquely interesting about just being in  the middle so for me it's not super  interesting and I don't pay too much  attention to it
 

